      "answer": "The customer whose issue started after the 2026-02-20 taxonomy rollout is BlueHarbor Logistics. Their problem was search relevance degradation in Event Nexus, with saved searches returning poor and duplicate results, increasing manual triage time to about 6 hours per day. This was triggered by the taxonomy rollout on 2026-02-20, as reported in the support ticket and confirmed in the renewal negotiation and retro documents.\n\nThe proof plan proposed to get BlueHarbor comfortable with renewal involves a short-term fix consisting of updating index weighting and adding a translation/mapping layer that maps new taxonomy terms to historical query tokens for the top 20 saved searches. The plan includes receiving schema registry export and query logs by 2026-03-19, starting an A/B test in staging on 2026-03-22 lasting 7-10 business days, with validation metrics requiring top-5 correct hit rate of at least 80%, no regression in suppression logic, and incident correlation latency under 200ms. If successful, a 1-day production rollout and 72-hour monitoring window will follow.\n\nA 90-day professional services engagement at a fixed price of $48,000 is offered to implement the tuning and run the proof, with a 30% discount if Orchestrator seat expansion is signed concurrently. A conditional credit clause is proposed: if the proof does not meet the agreed accuracy uplift within 10 business days, a one-quarter invoice credit prorated to the renewal will be applied.\n\nThis proof plan and commercial terms were discussed in detail during the renewal negotiation call and documented in the retro and competitor reports [art_8b0063fbb3cb, art_0bccc580184e, art_bd3560dfe194, art_c9970c1dc932].",
