      "answer": "The SCIM fields conflicting at Aureum were \"department\" and \"businessUnit.\" Merchant Services used \"businessUnit=merchant\" while Payments Ops used \"department=payments,\" causing ingestion normalization to fail to collapse these into a single canonical attribute. This led to the Rules Engine failing to match on the entity tag used to route approvals.\n\nJin proposed a fast fix to add a preprocessing rule in Signal Ingest to map \"businessUnit\" to \"department\" (or vice versa) and publish a normalized field for the correlator. This fix is a configuration-only change that can be hot-reloaded with low risk, avoiding the need to wait for Okta change control, which would take 2\u20134 weeks [art_79f625aafa16].",
