      "answer": "The customer most likely to defect to a cheaper tactical competitor if the next promised milestone is missed is Pioneer Freight Solutions. This is indicated by the detailed remediation plan and the commercial offer of a one-time credit of 10% ACV tied to milestone acceptance, reflecting high retention risk if milestones slip. The milestone in question is the acceptance milestone for the remediation plan addressing taxonomy change issues, specifically the acceptance by 2026-03-22 of the remediation plan steps including verification of schema registry compatibility and taxonomy snapshot collection. The full remediation plan includes subsequent steps such as shadow index build (2026-03-29 to 2026-04-09), backfill and recomputation (2026-04-12 to 2026-04-30), and validation window (2026-05-01 to 2026-05-14), but the critical milestone is the initial acceptance by 2026-03-22. Failure to meet this milestone triggers the 10% ACV credit and signals a high risk of the customer extending a tactical PoC with the competitor NoiseGuard, which is cheaper and easier to deploy but lacks the full automation and enrichment capabilities of Northstar's solution [art_7373b64fdfdd, art_ac8afb52f2d3]. \n\nNo other customer is explicitly linked to a similar high likelihood of defecting to a cheaper tactical competitor if milestones are missed, so Pioneer Freight Solutions is the only supported candidate for this risk [art_7373b64fdfdd].",
