      "answer": "Among the North America West Event Nexus accounts, the customers dealing with taxonomy/search semantics problems are Arcadia Cloudworks, BlueHarbor Logistics, CedarWind Renewables, HelioFab Systems, Pacific Health Network, and Pioneer Freight Solutions. These accounts report issues such as search relevance degradation, low-relevance or missing results, misfiring runbook triggers, and schema or index mapping problems following taxonomy updates.\n\nThe customers dealing with duplicate-action problems related to workflow deduplication drift during cross-system handoffs, often after acquisitions, are Helix Assemblies Inc., LedgerBright Analytics, LedgerPeak Software, MedLogix Distribution, Peregrine Logistics Group, and Pioneer Grid Retail LLC. These accounts report duplicate incidents, repeated remediation runs, idempotency key mismatches, and paging storms after system consolidations or event bridge integrations.\n\nThis classification is based on detailed support tickets describing the nature of the problems each customer faces. There is no explicit evidence that any account is dealing with both problem types simultaneously, nor is there explicit confirmation of the full list of North America West Event Nexus accounts beyond these 12 named customers, but the evidence assumes completeness for this cohort [art_90991e25335f, art_8b0063fbb3cb, art_10f7e8b72e09, art_9345d5653840, art_0ac4efa5a0ff, art_8478ccd5b200, art_2f780acc1f96, art_87b096c2c2d3, art_4eccfd9dcf29, art_0927b1cbb7f4, art_3ba29fe1e026, art_f64972a66eeb].",
